# ⚠️ THIS PACKAGE HAS MOVED

> ## `EulerApiSdk` is **deprecated** and no longer maintained.
>
> ## 👉 Use **[`TikTokApiSdk`](https://pypi.org/project/TikTokApiSdk/)** or **[`TikTokLiveApiSdk`](https://pypi.org/project/TikTokLiveApiSdk/)** instead.

`EulerApiSdk` is now two packages. Pick the one that fits:

| You want | Install | Import as |
|---|---|---|
| Everything: TikTok users, videos, OAuth, signing, captchas and the full TikTok LIVE API | [`TikTokApiSdk`](https://pypi.org/project/TikTokApiSdk/) | `TikTokApiSdk` |
| TikTok LIVE only | [`TikTokLiveApiSdk`](https://pypi.org/project/TikTokLiveApiSdk/) | `TikTokLiveApiSdk` |

`TikTokApiSdk` contains everything `EulerApiSdk` did, so it is the drop-in replacement.

## Migrating

Install the new package, then change the import name. The modules inside keep their names:

```bash
pip install TikTokApiSdk
```

```python
# before
from EulerApiSdk import AuthenticatedClient
from EulerApiSdk.api.tik_tok_users import retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic

# after
from TikTokApiSdk import AuthenticatedClient
from TikTokApiSdk.api.tik_tok_users import retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic
```

`EulerApiSdk` can stay installed while you switch, because it shares no files with the new packages. Remove it with `pip uninstall EulerApiSdk` once nothing imports it.

Nothing is being taken away: every published version of `EulerApiSdk` stays on PyPI, so projects pinned to one keep installing.

All future updates, bug fixes and new API coverage ship under the new names:

### 📦 https://pypi.org/project/TikTokApiSdk/

### 📦 https://pypi.org/project/TikTokLiveApiSdk/

> Unofficial: this project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to TikTok or ByteDance.

